# main.cjs: require("./inner.cjs"); require(globalThis.name)()   built with two entry points, main.cjs and other.cjs
# Of the program's own files a require() under a name that is put together at run time finds the entry points and no other, as in an executable that `bun build --compile` makes: the position gets what
# an entry point exports. A file that is in the image because another file names it by a constant is no answer, and a file that nothing names is not evaluated: the run time refuses both.
# No code that the build has not seen runs for that: a function that a module keeps to itself stays unreached
# RUN: valueflow-solve calls
